  "findingResponses": [
    "P1: Each of the exact eight class/surface/braking-or-turning/20mps identities maps uniquely to the independently read original d8f7d902 bytes. Recursive exactDeterministic requires every original key, finite number, boolean, vector, mechanics/material, settled/final four wheels and full curve/lateral data; extra/missing keys fail. Only top-level lifetime/readbacks are excluded and retain existing cleanup gates. No current-to-current comparison, new fixture or threshold. Native original28 validator/tick convention untouched.",
    "P2: causes uses guarded own property descriptors; no unsafe thrown-object property lookup, instanceof, String(object), getter, conversion hook, iterator, slice/map on thrown arrays or toJSON. Hostile accessors/traps/revoked proxies become UNKNOWN markers. 64 nodes/8 depth/64 child slots/8192 code units preserved; truncation explicit. Ordinary recordEvidence, raw/failure recordRun, factory recordFactoryFailure, terminal failTerminal and archive failure paths keep originals outside DTO serialization; thrown aggregates contain exact primary/cleanup/write references, including undefined.",
    "Audit: Native calibration entrypoint also consumes recordRun/failTerminal and thus the repaired serializer; native wheel-dynamics-fixture/disposeAfterFailure retain original references and explicit primaryFailed, no second serializer. Factory benchmark now uses the same testable helper. Browser calibration.ts instead uses CaptureLifetime.cause, whose existing String(error) conversion is separate from these native recording paths; inspected but NOT modified under numeric-reader/recording repair ownership. That broader browser lifecycle serializer remains an explicit parent-review limitation, not claimed safe by SOURCE10."
  ],
